<title>USA: FOB Gulf Grain - Nearby soy switches to August.</title>
<headline>FOB Gulf Grain - Nearby soy switches to August.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. FOB Gulf nearby soybean basis values switched to the August position early this week due to the volatility of the July/August spread on the Chicago Board of Trade, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;July could be really wild,&quot; one dealer said, referring to the volatility of the CBOT spot contract which was much higher in value than the August contract.</p>
<p>Dealers added that export activity was slow.</p>
<p>Corn slipped one cent a bushel while wheat values were unchanged.  </p>
